# Real student identifiers -- NEVER commit. functions/uids.json maps 30 Firebase UIDs to OpenStack
# project ids; it was produced while auditing the slot pool and sat UNTRACKED-BUT-COMMITTABLE for a
# day (git check-ignore matched nothing, so a stray `git add functions/` would have published real
# uids). Never committed -- verified with `git log --all -- functions/uids.json` = 0 commits.
# Archived at _archive/sensitive-untracked-2026-08-01/ rather than deleted.
functions/uids.json
functions/*-uids.json
functions/.scratch_verify/

# Scratch copies of functions/index.js left by QC runs. 370KB+ each, untracked and NOT ignored, so
# `git add -A` would have committed three near-duplicates of the entire functions source into the
# repo root. No literal credentials in them -- the "secret" hits are defineSecret() REFERENCES and
# header reads -- but they are still junk one command from being committed. (BUG-083 sweep)
.scratch_verify/
_tools/catalog.json

# Node inventory — real tailnet addresses. Public repo; belongs in hexworth-infra-private.
_docs/operations/compute-nodes-inventory.md

# Tooling-written safety copies (quiz keys, flag registry, rules probes). A machine
# writes these on a schedule, so they are gitignore rather than archive: there is no one-off
# question to preserve, and the noise hides the probes that DO need cleaning up.
functions/_backups/
